// Iron needs more heat, and raw ore leaves slag. Two lumps of raw iron ore in a smelter with its bellows driven by two
// counterweights: the heat climbs past iron's 1250 °C (copper's 1100 isn't enough for it), the ore melts to an
// ingot's worth (half an ingot a lump, raw), the mould against it casts an iron ingot, and the smelter lets out a
// lump of slag (half a lump for each lump of raw ore).
map
##################################
##################################
#....jj*jjjjjjj*.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............*.................#
#..............Y.................#
#..............Y.................#
#................................#
#................................#
#..........@........V............#
##################################
##################################

end
give Counterweight 2
give Smelter 1
place 2 -7 -8 Counterweight
place 2 -4 -7 Counterweight
place 3 7 -1 Smelter
drop 10 Coal 6 -7
drop 15 Coal 6 -7
drop 20 Coal 6 -7
drop 25 IronOre 6 -7
drop 30 IronOre 6 -7
expect 1200 smelttemp > 900
expect 1200 smelttemp < 1250          // not yet hot enough for iron...
expect 1200 smeltload == 2            // ...so the ore waits
expect 2400 smelttemp > 1250
expect 3600 smeltload == 0            // both melted
expect 3600 items:Slag == 1           // and the slag let out
expect 4800 items:IronIngot == 1      // cast and set
